se, both of which are simply translated copies of a fixed pattern. Because the maximum relative distance between particles is W, the transient before this blockage forms is at most W. The resulting periodic behavior has period 1 (if all cars move freely or are entirely jammed) or period 2 (if partially jammed). Rule 90 (XOR/additive) and Rule 110 (complex glider interactions) lack this conservation property and generate expanding Sierpinski-like patterns or Turing-complete interactions, ensuring that for certain initial states, the cycle length exceeds 2 or the transient exceeds 4*W.","optional_refs":[],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":[],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.65}],"simulation_proposals":[]}